// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 14-control-flow
// facility: rule.control.foreach (D-0042, D-0287); D-0135 (a view of a temporary used after its statement); conf.foreach-views-of-temporary
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.destroy-while-aliased (static)
//
// `foreach (t in StringView::split(StringView::trim(&f()), " "))`: the
// `String` that `f()` returns is a temporary of the loop's header, which
// ends before the loop's first round, while every part the loop takes is
// a view of it. The program is rejected before the run (D-0135), with a
// message that names the repair: bind the value, then walk views of the
// binding. (Before the session findings of 2026-11-06 the static pass
// could not see the loop's later use of its hidden holder, which has the
// `foreach`'s own position, and called the body decided: the compiled
// program read the freed bytes.)

import std;

fn make() : Result<String, String>
{
    Ok(String::copy("1.5 2.5\n"))
}

fn main()
{
    f64 sum = 0.0;
    foreach (tok in StringView::split(StringView::trim(&Result::unwrap(make())), " "))
    {
        match (StringView::parse<f64>(tok))
        {
            Ok(x)  : sum += x,
            Err(_) : {},
        }
    }
    printf("%v\n", sum);
}
